# Direct Database Queries

In the App Router, you can query directly in a Server Component (no need for `getServerSideProps`).

```jsx
// app/posts/page.js
export default async function PostsPage() {
  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany();
  return <ul>{posts.map(p => <li key={p.id}>{p.title}</li>)}</ul>;
}
```

No client code, no API route, no data fetching wrapper. It's just a function that runs on the server.

slides.codeSnippet:
// app/page.js
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';

export default async function Home() {
  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({
    take: 5,
    orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
  });

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Latest Posts</h1>
      <ul>
        {posts.map(post => <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </main>
  );
}

