# When the Client Needs Data

If you need to fetch data after user interaction (search, filter), you still create an API route that internally uses Prisma.

```js
// pages/api/posts.js
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';

export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany();
  res.json(posts);
}
```

Then the client calls `/api/posts` with fetch or SWR. The API route acts as a secure bridge.
